\[f(\theta + \pi) = \cos (\theta + \pi) = -\cos \theta = -r.\]In polar coordinates, the points $(r, \theta)$ and $(-r, \theta + \pi)$ coincide, so the graph repeats after an interval of $\pi.$

Therefore, the smallest possible value of $t$ is $\boxed{\pi}.$

